### Social Agent — Exemplos de Autenticação
### Compatível com a extensão REST Client (VS Code) e IntelliJ HTTP Client
### Substitua as variáveis antes de usar.

@base_url = http://localhost:8000/api/v1
@content_type = application/json


# ==============================================================================
# 1. REGISTRAR NOVA CONTA
# ==============================================================================
# POST /auth/register
# Body: JSON com email, password e full_name (opcional)
# Retorna: dados públicos do usuário (sem senha)
# Senha deve ter: ≥8 chars, 1 maiúscula, 1 minúscula, 1 número

POST {{base_url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{content_type}}

{
  "email": "joana@vitaforma.com.br",
  "password": "Vitaforma1",
  "full_name": "Joana Almeida"
}

###

# ==============================================================================
# 2. LOGIN (JSON — para frontends e apps mobile)
# ==============================================================================
# POST /auth/login
# Body: JSON com email e password
# Retorna: access_token, refresh_token, expires_in, user
# ► Salve access_token e refresh_token no cliente

POST {{base_url}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{content_type}}

{
  "email": "admin@vitaforma.com.br",
  "password": "admin123"
}

###

# ==============================================================================
# 3. LOGIN (OAuth2 form — compatível com Swagger UI)
# ==============================================================================
# POST /auth/token
# Body: form-encoded com username e password
# Retorna: { access_token, token_type }

POST {{base_url}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=admin@vitaforma.com.br&password=admin123

###

# ==============================================================================
# 4. MEU PERFIL
# ==============================================================================
# GET /auth/me
# Header: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
# Retorna: dados públicos do usuário autenticado

# ► Substitua <SEU_ACCESS_TOKEN> pelo token retornado no login
@access_token = COLE_SEU_ACCESS_TOKEN_AQUI

GET {{base_url}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

###

# ==============================================================================
# 5. ATUALIZAR PERFIL
# ==============================================================================
# PATCH /auth/me
# Header: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
# Body: JSON com full_name e/ou password (campos omitidos são preservados)

PATCH {{base_url}}/auth/me
Content-Type: {{content_type}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "full_name": "Joana Silva Almeida"
}

###

# ==============================================================================
# 6. RENOVAR TOKENS (quando access_token expirar)
# ==============================================================================
# POST /auth/refresh
# Body: JSON com refresh_token
# Retorna: novo par access_token + refresh_token + dados do usuário
# ► Atualize ambos os tokens armazenados no cliente

@refresh_token = COLE_SEU_REFRESH_TOKEN_AQUI

POST {{base_url}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{content_type}}

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refresh_token}}"
}

###

# ==============================================================================
# 7. TROCAR SENHA
# ==============================================================================
# POST /auth/change-password
# Header: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
# Body: JSON com current_password e new_password
# Retorna: 204 No Content (sem body)

POST {{base_url}}/auth/change-password
Content-Type: {{content_type}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "current_password": "Vitaforma1",
  "new_password": "NovaSenha2024!"
}

###

# ==============================================================================
# 8. USANDO O TOKEN EM OUTROS ENDPOINTS
# ==============================================================================
# Todos os endpoints protegidos seguem o mesmo padrão:
# Header: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>

# Exemplo: listar brands do usuário autenticado
GET {{base_url}}/brands
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

###

# Exemplo: criar uma brand
POST {{base_url}}/brands
Content-Type: {{content_type}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

{
  "name": "Minha Marca",
  "niche": "Fitness",
  "description": "Descrição da marca",
  "tone_of_voice": "Informal e motivador"
}

###

# ==============================================================================
# 9. ERROS ESPERADOS
# ==============================================================================

# 9a. Senha fraca no registro → 422 Unprocessable Entity
POST {{base_url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{content_type}}

{
  "email": "teste@email.com",
  "password": "fraca"
}

###

# 9b. E-mail duplicado → 409 Conflict
POST {{base_url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{content_type}}

{
  "email": "admin@vitaforma.com.br",
  "password": "Vitaforma1"
}

###

# 9c. Credenciais inválidas → 401 Unauthorized
POST {{base_url}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{content_type}}

{
  "email": "admin@vitaforma.com.br",
  "password": "senhaerrada"
}

###

# 9d. Token ausente → 401 Unauthorized
GET {{base_url}}/auth/me

###

# 9e. Refresh token expirado/inválido → 401 Unauthorized
POST {{base_url}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{content_type}}

{
  "refresh_token": "token.invalido.aqui"
}
